 "about_text": "Gallery Shukado is a Ginza art dealership founded in 2003 (as Art Office JC, renamed Shukado Co., Ltd. in 2006), now led by second-generation president Chiaki Tanaka. Based in a seventh-floor space in Ginza 6-chome, Tokyo, it deals in Japanese art from the Edo period to today, including nihonga and Western-style painting, calligraphy, rare books and ukiyo-e, alongside appraisal, cataloguing and export services. In 2016 it launched SHUKADO CONTEMPORARY to promote younger artists, and in 2022 opened GALLERY SCENA in Harajuku for contemporary art. The gallery exhibits regularly at fairs in Japan and abroad.",
 "source_kind": "official",
